{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And he turned this way and that.</b> He saw what he did to him in the house and what he did to him in the field.<br><br><b>And he saw that there was no man.</b> There was no man destined to arise from him who would convert.<br><b>And he struck the Egyptian.</b> Moses was worthy, from the six days of creation, to perform this deed — to kill the Egyptian — for the strength of the Egyptian is the strength of Cain, which is from the side of impurity. And from this the Sages, of blessed memory, said: the slaughter of a non-Jew is a nevelah and imparts impurity by carrying, for the impurity stems from his force. And understand this." "<b>And know</b> that this striking was by speech, for he killed him with the breath of his lips. And so the Sages, of blessed memory, interpreted: he killed him with the Explicit Name. And the proof is from what is written: ״הלהרגני אתה אומר״ — 'Do you mean to kill me?' — by speech alone, and it was the Explicit Name of 42 letters. And there is in the verse a provocation regarding this. And so David, of blessed memory, said (Psalms 44:6): ״בך צרינו ננגח בשמך נבוס קמינו״ — and he said this concerning the 42 letters. And concerning this it is said (Psalms 148:13): ״כי נשגב שמו לבדו״, and this is ״כי הוא אמר ויהי״, and this is (Job 26:7): ״תולה ארץ על בלימה״. And understand this. And by the power of this Name Moses said: עלה שור, עלה שור. And so we find with Elisha the prophet, concerning those lads who mocked him and said to him (II Kings 2:23): ״עלה קרח עלה קרח״ — Scripture mentions concerning him: ״ויפן אחריו ויראם ויקללם בשם ה׳״ — and that is the Name of 42 letters, and therefore 42 children were killed, as it is written (ibid.): ״ותצאנה שתים דובים מן היער ותבקענה מהם מבנים ארבעים ושנים״. And the expression ויך את המצרי comes in the same sense as (II Kings 19:35): ״ויצא מלאך ה׳ ויך במחנה אשור״ — the intention is not a striking with the hand but a striking of force." "<b>And he hid him in the sand.</b> He said to Israel: you are compared to sand, as it is said (Hosea 1): ״והיה מספר בני ישראל כחול הים״. This sand — a person takes it from here and places it there, and no sound goes forth; so too the matter would not be heard."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {1 "Source cites Psalms 44:6 and 148:13; II Kings 2:23–24 and 19:35; Job 26:7. All normalized to standard chapter:verse. The citation of II Kings 2:24 for '42 children' is implicit in his reading of verse 23."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:55:24.856352275Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}